WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.278 --> 00:00:03.367
The original goal was not simply to send a

2
00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:06.856
reminder. It was to help a person receive information

3
00:00:06.878 --> 00:00:09.922
they can understand and use to take the next

4
00:00:09.944 --> 00:00:13.678
step. That purpose should guide how the team learns

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.344
from an authorized change.

6
00:00:16.118 --> 00:00:18.762
A count of reminders sent tells you that an

7
00:00:18.784 --> 00:00:22.029
activity occurred. It does not by itself show that

8
00:00:22.051 --> 00:00:26.896
messages were received, understood, accessible or useful. Those are

9
00:00:26.918 --> 00:00:29.673
different questions, and each may need a different source

10
00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:30.407
of information.

11
00:00:31.226 --> 00:00:34.559
For your own work, return to the purpose you

12
00:00:34.581 --> 00:00:38.670
named at the beginning. What experience or result did

13
00:00:38.692 --> 00:00:41.826
the change aim to improve? What would you need

14
00:00:41.848 --> 00:00:44.648
to learn before saying that it helped, and for

15
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.048
whom?

16
00:00:46.384 --> 00:00:50.429
Consider a process question: were reminders prepared and sent

17
00:00:50.451 --> 00:00:54.607
using the authorized method? Consider an experience question: could

18
00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:57.629
people understand the message and find help? Consider an

19
00:00:57.651 --> 00:01:01.029
outcome question: did people have a usable opportunity to

20
00:01:01.051 --> 00:01:02.451
take the intended next step?

21
00:01:02.973 --> 00:01:06.751
You may not have answers to all three. Identify

22
00:01:06.773 --> 00:01:10.373
what is available, the period it covers, who is

23
00:01:10.396 --> 00:01:13.262
responsible for it and whether you are authorized to

24
00:01:13.284 --> 00:01:16.462
use it. Where a starting point or comparison has

25
00:01:16.484 --> 00:01:20.018
not been established, record that as a gap instead

26
00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:21.151
of creating a number.

27
00:01:22.084 --> 00:01:25.396
The evaluation-plan worksheet can help connect a question, source,

28
00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:29.684
responsible role, review point and possible next decision. Its

29
00:01:30.373 --> 00:01:33.707
notes are not automatically saved; copy or download them

30
00:01:33.729 --> 00:01:35.618
if you want to keep a general working note.

31
00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.173
Follow the instructions shown in the worksheet.

32
00:01:39.118 --> 00:01:42.340
Suppose a team later sees a higher response count.

33
00:01:42.673 --> 00:01:45.140
That could be worth exploring, but the count alone

34
00:01:45.162 --> 00:01:49.029
cannot establish that a particular communication change caused it

35
00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:52.784
or that everyone could participate. Timing, outreach, the number

36
00:01:52.807 --> 00:01:55.940
of people contacted and other conditions could also matter.

37
00:01:56.573 --> 00:01:59.684
Look at both numbers and people's accounts where those

38
00:01:59.707 --> 00:02:03.662
sources are appropriate and authorized. Ask who may be

39
00:02:03.684 --> 00:02:06.684
missing from the information and what the evidence cannot

40
00:02:06.707 --> 00:02:10.284
show. Do not infer an individual's identity or treat

41
00:02:10.307 --> 00:02:13.329
a small group as anonymous without the responsible data

42
00:02:13.351 --> 00:02:14.173
owner's guidance.

43
00:02:15.024 --> 00:02:19.447
Protect private information. Agree reporting, access and disclosure rules

44
00:02:19.469 --> 00:02:22.869
with the responsible office before gathering or sharing data.

45
00:02:22.891 --> 00:02:26.869
Do not paste names, appointment details, case information, health

46
00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:30.136
information or personnel records into learning notes.

47
00:02:31.258 --> 00:02:35.769
Identify the role responsible for reviewing the information, the

48
00:02:35.791 --> 00:02:38.169
proposed time to return to it and the decision

49
00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:41.102
that the review could inform. These are plans to

50
00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:44.769
confirm, not commitments to invent on someone else's behalf.

51
00:02:45.408 --> 00:02:48.341
For the reminder example, the team might agree to

52
00:02:48.363 --> 00:02:51.674
look at delivery and assistance questions after an authorized

53
00:02:51.697 --> 00:02:55.630
change, while also seeking appropriate feedback about whether the

54
00:02:55.652 --> 00:02:59.186
message was usable. If a help route remains unclear

55
00:02:59.630 --> 00:03:02.430
or an authorized method is not working, the team

56
00:03:02.452 --> 00:03:05.541
can bring that concern back to the responsible reviewers.

57
00:03:06.401 --> 00:03:09.379
Share what can appropriately be shared with people who

58
00:03:09.401 --> 00:03:12.868
contributed: what was learned, what changed, what did not

59
00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:16.690
change and what remains unresolved. Report-back is part of

60
00:03:16.712 --> 00:03:20.468
respectful participation, not a promise to accept every suggestion.

61
00:03:21.746 --> 00:03:25.012
In the activity below, consider what a change in

62
00:03:25.034 --> 00:03:29.012
the reminder count can and cannot establish. Choose a

63
00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:32.412
response, then read the feedback and compare the reasoning.

64
00:03:32.968 --> 00:03:35.523
The activity is a learning aid; it does not

65
00:03:35.546 --> 00:03:37.946
make a conclusion about an actual service.

66
00:03:38.501 --> 00:03:42.434
For your own example, write one process question, one

67
00:03:42.457 --> 00:03:46.479
question about experience, a possible information source and the

68
00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.457
role that could review it. If any source, comparison

69
00:03:49.479 --> 00:03:52.634
or review date is not yet agreed, mark it

70
00:03:52.657 --> 00:03:53.968
as a question to resolve.

71
00:03:55.037 --> 00:03:58.192
You began by defining a decision and its purpose.

72
00:03:58.792 --> 00:04:02.726
You considered the appropriate depth, requirements, affected people, evidence

73
00:04:02.837 --> 00:04:06.037
and alternatives. You prepared a recommendation for the responsible

74
00:04:06.059 --> 00:04:09.770
review, planned an authorized change and identified how to

75
00:04:09.792 --> 00:04:10.770
learn from the result.

76
00:04:11.448 --> 00:04:15.848
Return to the existing toolkit, policy, engagement resources and

77
00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.981
evaluation plan whenever they are useful. The point is

78
00:04:19.003 --> 00:04:21.337
not to complete every form. It is to make

79
00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:25.203
a responsible decision more understandable, inclusive and open to

80
00:04:25.226 --> 00:04:28.492
improvement through the people and processes that actually govern

81
00:04:28.514 --> 00:04:28.981
the work.
